    {
      "id": "rh5xM7pd8haFGsfC-d9pV",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 266.9536772691173,
      "y": -398.31999065379114,
      "width": 2496.96630859375,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 155053539,
      "version": 1606,
      "versionNonce": 1320255523,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1737811724882,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. I need data(contact) container which has index. also this container should be not static.... std::vector is reasonable\n2. Using std::vector allow us to use std:algorithm which gives plenty of efficient algorithm like add, delete, sort, seach,...\n3. So Phonebook class has data container as class member. and that class member is vector\n4. There may be two options. \n    1)First is set this vectort's element type as another vecotr contains name and bookmark number and nickname as appropriate type( std::string)\n    2)Second is set vector type as another class(contact) which hass class member as name and bookmark etc.. this has more advantage because these element can be any type.\n\n\n\nthis program implements first option(ver1) maybe next time ver2 when I get used to using Class...",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 340,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. I need data(contact) container which has index. also this container should be not static.... std::vector is reasonable\n2. Using std::vector allow us to use std:algorithm which gives plenty of efficient algorithm like add, delete, sort, seach,...\n3. So Phonebook class has data container as class member. and that class member is vector\n4. There may be two options. \n    1)First is set this vectort's element type as another vecotr contains name and bookmark number and nickname as appropriate type( std::string)\n    2)Second is set vector type as another class(contact) which hass class member as name and bookmark etc.. this has more advantage because these element can be any type.\n\n\n\nthis program implements first option(ver1) maybe next time ver2 when I get used to using Class...",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
